{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792773877,"nonce":"CKx8FRfzoaniPAAYCrQeXC8fL3s=","title":"Scroll containers: public reach signals and an option that draws the edge shadows","message":"Requested by the ChimpMonk editor (its c5dcac7). It marks each scroll container once a frame with data-more-above and data-more-below to draw inset shadows at an edge that hides content, walking Scroll.byNode with @:privateAccess, because ashui has no public way to enumerate scroll containers and Scroll.limits() is not reactive.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\nA reactive reach on every Scroll (more content above, below, left, right), and an option, a CSS property such as scroll-shadow with --ui-scroll-shadow-color, that draws the shadows at an edge that hides content, so no app has to. A public enumerator of containers only if the option is not enough.","files":null}]}